<Base title="Privacy notice | MedPally Find" description="How MedPally Find handles personal data."><main id="main" class="shell legal"><p class="legal-date">Last updated 27 October 2026</p><h1>Privacy notice</h1>
<p class="legal-lead">MedPally Find is a public directory with no accounts and no analytics. This notice explains the small amount of data that is still involved when you visit.</p>
<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>MedPally Find (find.medpally.com) is run by Marlo Solutions Ltd, a company registered in England and Wales under company number 17309992. We are the data controller for personal data processed through this website.</p>
<address>Suite RA01<br/>195–197 Wood Street<br/>London<br/>E17 3NU<br/>United Kingdom</address>
<p>Contact us about anything in this notice at <a href="mailto:hello@marlosolutions.com">hello@marlosolutions.com</a>.</p>
<h2>What we collect</h2>
<p>This website does not set cookies, run analytics, use tracking technologies or ask you to sign up. Searching and filtering happen in your browser; your searches are not sent to us.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hosting logs.</strong> The site is hosted by Cloudflare, which may record standard request data, including IP addresses, for security and operational purposes. We do not use these logs to identify visitors.</li>
<li><strong>Website logos.</strong> The logo on each listing is loaded from Google's favicon service. When your browser loads those images, Google receives your IP address and the web addresses of the listed sites, under Google's own privacy policy.</li>
<li><strong>Saved resources.</strong> When you save a resource, its listing ID is stored in your browser's local storage on your device. It is not sent to us, and you can clear it at any time by removing the saved items or clearing this site's data in your browser.</li>
<li><strong>Suggestions.</strong> When you use the suggest form, we receive the link and note you send, and your IP address, which we use briefly to limit repeated submissions. The link and note are posted as a public issue in our GitHub repository so we can review them; they are not linked to your IP address there. The form uses Cloudflare Turnstile to check that you are not a bot; Turnstile processes information about your browser and connection under Cloudflare's privacy policy.</li>
<li><strong>Emails.</strong> If you email us to suggest a resource or ask for a listing to be corrected or removed, we receive your email address, your name if you include it, and your message.</li>
<li><strong>Listings.</strong> Listings may name the person or organisation that made a resource, using information they have published themselves. If you are named and want the entry changed or removed, email us.</li>
</ul>
<h2>How we use it</h2>
<p>We use emails to reply to you and act on your request, suggestions to decide what to add, and listing information to run the directory. Our legal basis is our legitimate interest in operating the directory and responding to people who contact us (Article 6(1)(f) UK GDPR). We do not use your data for marketing, build profiles or sell personal data.</p>
<h2>Sharing and international transfers</h2>
<p>We share data only with the providers that run our hosting (Cloudflare), email and code repository (GitHub). They process data on our behalf under their own contractual and legal obligations. Where a provider processes data outside the UK, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as adequacy regulations or standard contractual clauses.</p>
<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>We keep emails for as long as needed to deal with your request, then delete them. Suggestions stay in the public GitHub repository as a record of what was proposed; email us if you want one removed. Hosting logs are kept according to Cloudflare's standard retention periods.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to access, correct or delete your personal data, object to or restrict how we use it, and receive it in a portable format. Email <a href="mailto:hello@marlosolutions.com">hello@marlosolutions.com</a> to do so. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>
<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this changes, for example if we add accounts, we will update this notice and the date at the top.</p>
</main></Base>
